    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: First-Time Visitors Rainy-Day Planning</h1>
    <p>Rain in Hanoi is not an interruption of riding season; it is part of it. The city's wet months deliver their water in dramatic, often predictable bursts, streets run shiny, drainage works hard, and the whole riding population simply adjusts: slower, drier and patient. First-time visitors who plan for rain the way they plan for traffic, with knowledge, gear and a willingness to wait, lose almost nothing to it. The ones who don't learn wet-riding lessons the expensive way. This guide is the planning.</p>
    <p>This page belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> series for first-time visitors, focused strictly on wet-condition planning. The full seasonal picture is on the <a href="/motorbike-guides/best-time-to-ride-motorbike-hanoi/">best-time-to-ride guide</a>, the deep wet-road craft on the <a href="/motorbike-guides/riding-a-motorbike-in-hanoi-rainy-season/">rainy season riding guide</a>, and the verified prices for every machine on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, with the general rental questions on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
